troski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.1511286847422453,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":83.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.13944511499191625,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":94.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.08509380234910902,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":67.5,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08353221766452719,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08342865222461815,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004350269863009581,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.38502997,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"USA Compression Partners, LP provides natural gas compression services in the United States. The company offers compression services to oil companies and independent producers, processors, gatherers, and transporters of natural gas and crude oil, as well as for infrastructure applications, including centralized natural gas gathering systems and processing facilities, and gas lift applications in crude oil wells. It also owns and operates a fleet of equipment to offer natural gas treating services, such as carbon dioxide and hydrogen sulfide removal, as well as natural gas cooling and dehydration to natural gas producers and midstream companies. As of December 31, 2025, the company has 3.9 million horsepower in its fleet. USA Compression Partners, LP was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Micah C. Green | President & CEO of USA Compression GP LLC | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 885 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $313K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["USA Compression Partners, LP is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.6B market cap on $998M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","The business throws off $277M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 28 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 39% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 32% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3217665615141956},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (75% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"USA Compression Partners (NYSE:USAC) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Meets Expectations","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/usa-compression-partners-nyseusac-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-meets-expectations.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793810457.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Compared to Estimates, USA Compression (USAC) Q3 Earnings: A Look at Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks